  "summary": "Enter x , y DT pairs (≥2), AC, then recall A, B, and r. Fitted curve: y = A e^(Bx).",
  "body": [
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Exp fits y = A e^(Bx). Positive B gives growth that speeds up; negative B gives decay toward zero. Use when percentage change is roughly constant (population growth, radioactive decay)."
    },
    {
      "type": "formula",
      "plain": "y = A e^{Bx}"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "mark": "reg-graph",
      "text": "Exponential regression fits y = A e^(Bx). Positive B gives growth that speeds up; negative B gives decay toward zero. On semi-log paper (ln y vs x) the same data would look straight."
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "mark": "reg-graph",
      "svg": "img/reg/exp.svg",
      "caption": "Sample fit y = 2 e^(0.5x). Each equal step in x multiplies y by about e^0.5 ≈ 1.65."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Input"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Open Exp regression, clear old data, enter at least two pairs as x , y DT. For a decay model, y values are usually positive."
    },
    {
      "type": "keys",
      "keys": [
        "MODE",
        "5",
        "3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "steps",
      "title": "Enter data",
      "items": [
        "SHIFT 9 → 1 EXE if replacing an old list",
        "For each point: x , y DT",
        "AC when finished"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "lines",
      "lead": "Example — four points on y = 2 e^(0.5x):",
      "items": [
        "0 , 2 DT",
        "1 , 3.3 DT",
        "2 , 5.44 DT",
        "3 , 8.96 DT",
        "AC"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "text": "Minimum 2 pairs. The model uses ln y internally; all y values should be positive for a real fit."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Output"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "After AC, recall A (initial scale), B (growth rate in the exponent), and r. The fitted equation is y = A e^(Bx)."
    },
    {
      "type": "lines",
      "lead": "S-VAR recalls (after AC):",
      "items": [
        "A — SHIFT 2 → 1 → ▶ → ▶ → 1 EXE",
        "B — SHIFT 2 → 1 → ▶ → ▶ → 2 EXE",
        "r — SHIFT 2 → 1 → ▶ → ▶ → 3 EXE",
        "ŷ for a given x: type x, SHIFT 2 → 1 → ◀ → 2 EXE",
        "x̂ for a given y (> 0): type y, SHIFT 2 → 1 → ◀ → 1 EXE"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Worked example"
    },
    {
